**Answer**

The probability that at least one of four fair six‑sided dice shows a six is  

\[
P(\text{at least one six}) \;=\; 1-\left(\frac{5}{6}\right)^{4}
\;=\; 1-\frac{625}{1296}
\;=\; \frac{671}{1296}
\;\approx\;0.5177\;(51.8\%).
\]

